<title>TURKEY: Turkish Tupras Q1 losses surge.</title>
<headline>Turkish Tupras Q1 losses surge.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share loss   (lira) 5,752.93 vs     383.82</p>
<p>    Loss			 26,877.70 vs   1,793.20</p>
<p>    Net sales		 120 057.21 vs  57,049.13</p>
<p>    Operating loss	   25,268.95 vs   3,569.52</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  714.95 vs   2,111.20</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 949.20 vs	56.13</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     1,384.47 vs     269.69</p>
<p>    Total debts	     158,099.71 vs  65,567.50</p>
<p>    Equity		    (11,381.62)vs  18,638.15</p>
<p>    Capital		     4,672.00 vs   4,672.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish oil refiner Tupras-Turkiye Petrol Rafinerileri A.S. is slated for privatisation with 96.41 percent of its capital held by the privatisation administration OIB.</p>
<p>The company plans to raise its capital to 29.9 trillion lira by issuing 2.7 bonuses and 2.7 rights for one existing share, subject to approval by the OIB and the Capital Markets Board. Its 1996 loss was 18.97 trillion lira.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
